Feature: let the application own the guest output (native renderer hand-off)

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk)
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0004-external-guest-output.patch
Status:     local patch, not upstream yet (small, generic: worth proposing)

WHAT WAS MISSING
  The port is growing its own Vulkan renderer (docs/04-native-renderer.md,
  docs/findings/08). Its frames reach the window the same way the emulated
  GPU's do: Presenter::RefreshGuestOutput(), which hands a callback the
  "guest output" image. But the emulated GPU keeps running during
  development ("shadow mode": the game's original renderer runs, ours
  mirrors it), and every one of its swaps refreshes the guest output too.
  Two producers, one image: the picture would flicker between both.

THE CHANGE
  * Presenter::SetGuestOutputExternal(bool) / IsGuestOutputExternal()
    (include/rex/ui/presenter.h): an atomic flag, set by the application
    while its own renderer provides the picture.
  * Vulkan and D3D12 IssueSwap (src/graphics/*/command_processor.cpp): when
    the flag is set, end the frame right after BeginSubmission, without
    refreshing the guest output. This is the same early exit the Vulkan
    backend already takes for frames it chooses not to present (the async
    shader placeholder path), so per-frame bookkeeping is unchanged.
  Flag off (the default) = exactly the old behavior.

HOW IT'S USED
  src/native/native_renderer.cpp: F9 (bind_renderer) switches the window
  between the emulated picture and the native one; the flag follows it.
---
diff --git a/include/rex/ui/presenter.h b/include/rex/ui/presenter.h
index afb4a30..3326c93 100644
--- a/include/rex/ui/presenter.h
+++ b/include/rex/ui/presenter.h
@@ -358,6 +358,18 @@ class Presenter {
   bool RefreshGuestOutput(uint32_t frontbuffer_width, uint32_t frontbuffer_height,
                           uint32_t display_aspect_ratio_x, uint32_t display_aspect_ratio_y,
                           std::function<bool(GuestOutputRefreshContext& context)> refresher);
+  // External guest output: an application with its own host renderer (a
+  // native port replacing the emulated GPU's picture) sets this while its own
+  // RefreshGuestOutput calls provide the picture. GPU emulation then skips
+  // refreshing the guest output on its swaps (it still ends the frame as
+  // usual), so the two producers don't overwrite each other. Any thread.
+  void SetGuestOutputExternal(bool external) {
+    guest_output_external_.store(external, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+  }
+  bool IsGuestOutputExternal() const {
+    return guest_output_external_.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+  }
+
   // The implementation must be callable from any thread, including from
   // multiple at the same time, and it should acquire the latest guest output
   // image via ConsumeGuestOutput.
@@ -937,6 +949,9 @@ class Presenter {
   // UI thread: writable, guest output thread: read-only.
   GuestOutputPaintConfig guest_output_paint_config_;
 
+  // See SetGuestOutputExternal.
+  std::atomic<bool> guest_output_external_{false};
+
   // Single-producer-multiple-consumers (lock-free SPSC + consumer lock) mailbox
   // for presenting of the most up-to-date guest output image without long
   // interlocking between guest output refreshing and painting.
diff --git a/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp b/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp
index 19874a5..7f51e19 100644
--- a/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp
@@ -1911,6 +1911,14 @@ void D3D12CommandProcessor::IssueSwap(uint32_t frontbuffer_ptr, uint32_t frontbu
     return;
   }
 
+  // The application's own renderer provides the picture right now: end the
+  // frame without refreshing the guest output (see
+  // Presenter::SetGuestOutputExternal).
+  if (presenter->IsGuestOutputExternal()) {
+    EndSubmission(true);
+    return;
+  }
+
   // Obtain the actual swap source texture size (resolution-scaled if it's a
   // resolve destination, or not otherwise).
   D3D12_SHADER_RESOURCE_VIEW_DESC swap_texture_srv_desc;
diff --git a/src/graphics/vulkan/command_processor.cpp b/src/graphics/vulkan/command_processor.cpp
index 001f36b..1f459cb 100644
--- a/src/graphics/vulkan/command_processor.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/vulkan/command_processor.cpp
@@ -2289,6 +2289,14 @@ void VulkanCommandProcessor::IssueSwap(uint32_t frontbuffer_ptr, uint32_t frontb
     return;
   }
 
+  // The application's own renderer provides the picture right now: end the
+  // frame like the other skipped-presentation path below, without refreshing
+  // the guest output.
+  if (presenter->IsGuestOutputExternal()) {
+    EndSubmission(true);
+    return;
+  }
+
   bool skip_present_due_async_placeholder = REXCVAR_GET(async_shader_compilation) &&
                                             REXCVAR_GET(vulkan_async_skip_incomplete_frames) &&
                                             frame_used_async_placeholder_pipeline_;
